{
  "content": {
    "body": "This is the BASE component catalog for a **structure** pebble — an IN-CODE\ndata shape: a DTO, a type/interface, a request/response or wire body, a\nconfig or return type. NOT a persisted database table (that is a\n`model`). It DEFINES every component (category) and WHAT belongs under it;\nother knowledge and skills — extraction, verification, fix — REFERENCE\nthis to learn what goes under `name`, `type`, a `ref`, etc. They own the\nMETHOD; this doc owns the DEFINITIONS.\n\nA structure is the sibling of a model, with a DIFFERENT set of fields: it\nhas NO primary key, NO reference key (FK), NO default and NO relationships\n— those are DB/model concepts. Truth for a structure is the SOURCE CODE\n(the type/class/interface), not a DDL.\n\nRead each entry as: the component, then the values/shape considered part\nof it.\n\n## Pebble-level components\n\n- **name** — the shape's identifier. Under it: one string equal to the\n  type / class / interface / DTO name in the codebase.\n- **status** — spec↔code alignment. Under it: ONE of — planned ·\n  in-progress · implemented · verified · drift · broken · missing ·\n  deprecated.\n- **description** — prose. Under it: what the shape represents and where it\n  is used (the endpoint/DTO/config it backs).\n- **checklist reference** — a link to a checklist pebble. Under it: the\n  requirement / acceptance items that gate an implement / verify / fix.\n  Present only when there is such an intent.\n- **structure references** — pebble→pebble edges to OTHER **structure**\n  pebbles. Under it: every structure this one nests or points at (from\n  `ref` fields), captured in both directions. A structure references ONLY\n  structures — never models.\n- **findings references** — links to finding pebbles. Under it: dated,\n  append-only evidence for anything that does not meet spec.\n- **resources** — the structure's ENTRY POINTS into the codebase (code\n  links). PURPOSE: a resource tells the AI the EXACT file — optionally a\n  symbol and line — to open FIRST when it needs to investigate, understand,\n  verify or fix this shape, so it starts from the real code instead of\n  re-discovering where the type lives. Whenever the AI reads a source file\n  that defines or uses this structure (its type / interface / DTO), it\n  SHOULD link it here so later discovery is instant. Find the file with the\n  code map (`map-search` / `map-file` / `map-symbol`) — the user does the\n  same via the app's Mapping feature — then bind with `link-code` (remove\n  with `unlink-code`). Under it: a list of { path, symbol?, line?, note? }.\n  Resources point at CODE — NOT at other pebbles the way references do.\n\nA structure references exactly THREE things, in this order: a **checklist**\n(the requirement gate — listed first), other **structures**, and\n**findings**. It has NO model references and NO relationships, and rules\nare NOT a component of it. (Resources are code links, not references.)\n\n## Field / property components — the categories under each\n\n- **name** — the property identifier. Under it: one string matching the\n  code.\n- **type** — the property's shape type. Under it, ONE of:\n  - a **primitive**: string · number · integer · float · boolean · date ·\n    datetime · timestamp · uuid · email · url · null · any;\n  - a **composite**: `object` (its properties live in `children`) or\n    `array` (its element type is `itemType`; when that is `object`, the\n    element's properties live in `children`);\n  - a **ref** → another **structure** pebble (carried in `typeRef`; that\n    structure's name becomes the display type).\n- **itemType** (`array` only) — the element's type. Under it: the same\n  vocabulary as `type` (including `object` and `ref`).\n- **required** — a boolean. Under it: whether the property is REQUIRED in\n  the shape. NOTE this is a plain optional/required flag — NOT a database\n  NOT-NULL (a structure has no DB semantics).\n- **accepted** — the value whitelist. Under it: the ONE-OR-MORE specific\n  values this property is allowed to hold — this is where ENUMS and every\n  value-constrained field live (status sets, kinds, modes, currency codes,\n  …), captured as a LIST of strings. Empty/absent = any value. A `sample`\n  (and any concrete value) MUST be one of the accepted values; on an\n  `array` it constrains each element. The CLI rejects a malformed list or a\n  sample that falls outside it.\n- **sample** — optional. Under it: one example value, verbatim\n  (\"john@acme.io\", \"42\", \"true\") — feeds generated example payloads.\n- **status** — the property's spec↔code alignment. Under it: the SAME\n  status vocabulary as the pebble.\n- **description** — prose. Under it: the property's meaning, unit, allowed\n  values, gotchas.\n- **children** — nested properties. Under it: an `object`'s properties, or\n  (for an `array` whose element is an object) the element's properties.\n\n## Reference — the one kind a structure captures\n\nA structure connects only to OTHER structures: a field whose `type` (or an\narray's `itemType`) is `ref` carries a `typeRef` pointing at the target\nstructure pebble. It is captured as a pebble→pebble edge in **structure\nreferences**, in both directions, at ANY nesting depth. There is no FK and\nno relationship — those belong to models.\n\n## Structure vs model\n\n- **model** — a persisted DB table (truth = the DDL). DB column types, a\n  primary key, reference keys (FKs), NOT-NULL (nullable), defaults, and\n  relationships. References other models.\n- **structure** — an in-code shape (truth = the source). Shape types with\n  nesting, a plain required flag, accepted values, sample values, and refs\n  to other structures. No PK / FK / NOT-NULL / default / relationships.\n  References only structures.\n\nClassifying a persisted table as a structure (or a DTO as a model) is a\ndefect — fix the section, don't force the fields.\n\n## Quick map — category → what's under it\n\n| Component | Under it (shape / allowed values) |\n|---|---|\n| pebble.name | type / DTO / interface name (string) |\n| pebble.status | planned·in-progress·implemented·verified·drift·broken·missing·deprecated |\n| pebble.description | prose: what the shape is + where used |\n| checklist reference | link → checklist pebble (requirement items) |\n| structure references | edges → other structure pebbles (from ref fields) |\n| findings references | links → finding pebbles |\n| resources | code links → { path, symbol?, line?, note? } to the defining source |\n| field.name | property name (string) |\n| field.type | primitive · object · array · ref (→ structure) |\n| field.itemType | (array) element type — same vocabulary |\n| field.required | boolean (required in the shape; NOT a DB NOT-NULL) |\n| field.accepted | enum / value whitelist — one or more allowed strings (a sample must be one of them), or any |\n| field.sample | one verbatim example value |\n| field.status | same status vocabulary |\n| field.description | prose |\n| field.children | nested properties (object props / array-of-object element props) |\n\n## Structure CLI — all structure pebble operations live here\n\nEvery structure mutation goes through `pebbles-cli` (never hand-edit\n`.pebble` files). A structure's content kind is **schema** (a nested field\ntree). `content` is sent WHOLE. The write is HARDENED:\n\n- a `ref` field's `typeRef` is auto-captured at ANY depth — the CLI\n  resolves the target structure's real `pebbleId` and mirrors the edge at\n  the pebble level, so both structures show the connection in `refs`;\n- **accepted** values are validated: when present it must be a non-empty\n  list of non-empty strings, and a field's `sample` must be one of them —\n  a malformed list or an out-of-set sample is rejected;\n- a link whose target does not exist is DROPPED and reported in\n  `droppedRefs` — create the target structure first;\n- there is NO delete: retire a structure with status `deprecated`.\n\nCREATE — a structure with a primitive, an object (children), an array, and\na ref to another structure:\n\n    pebbles-cli create structures --title \"Customer DTO\" --content '{\n      \"kind\": \"schema\",\n      \"fields\": [\n        { \"name\": \"id\", \"type\": \"uuid\", \"required\": true,\n          \"status\": \"implemented\", \"description\": \"Customer id\" },\n        { \"name\": \"email\", \"type\": \"email\", \"required\": true,\n          \"status\": \"implemented\", \"description\": \"Contact email\",\n          \"sample\": \"jo@acme.io\" },\n        { \"name\": \"tier\", \"type\": \"string\", \"required\": false,\n          \"accepted\": [\"free\", \"pro\", \"enterprise\"], \"status\": \"implemented\",\n          \"description\": \"Plan tier\" },\n        { \"name\": \"billing\", \"type\": \"ref\", \"required\": true,\n          \"status\": \"implemented\", \"description\": \"Billing address\",\n          \"typeRef\": { \"path\": \"structures/address-dto.pebble\" } },\n        { \"name\": \"meta\", \"type\": \"object\", \"required\": false,\n          \"status\": \"implemented\", \"description\": \"Freeform metadata\",\n          \"children\": [\n            { \"name\": \"source\", \"type\": \"string\", \"required\": false,\n              \"status\": \"implemented\", \"description\": \"Acquisition source\" }\n          ] },\n        { \"name\": \"tags\", \"type\": \"array\", \"itemType\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": false, \"status\": \"implemented\",\n          \"description\": \"Freeform labels\" }\n      ]\n    }'\n\nUPDATE — top-level keys merge; `content` is replaced WHOLE (send the full\nfield tree). Units match by id, or by name when a unit has no id:\n\n    pebbles-cli update structures/customer-dto.pebble --patch '{ \"description\": \"The customer payload returned by the API\", \"content\": { \"kind\": \"schema\", \"fields\": [ ...full tree... ] } }'\n\nSTATUS — per field or whole structure:\n\n    pebbles-cli set-status structures/customer-dto.pebble verified --unit <fieldId>\n    pebbles-cli set-status structures/customer-dto.pebble drift\n\nFINDING — evidence when a component doesn't meet spec:\n\n    pebbles-cli add-finding structures/customer-dto.pebble --title \"tier accepts unlisted value\" --category spec-violation --body \"API returns tier=trial, not in the accepted set (free|pro|enterprise)\"\n\nINSPECT — connections both ways (structure ref edges + backlinks), read,\nvalidate:\n\n    pebbles-cli refs structures/customer-dto.pebble\n    pebbles-cli get structures/customer-dto.pebble\n    pebbles-cli validate structures/customer-dto.pebble\n\nRESOURCES — link the source that defines the shape:\n\n    pebbles-cli link-code structures/customer-dto.pebble --file app/DTO/CustomerDTO.php --symbol CustomerDTO\n    pebbles-cli unlink-code structures/customer-dto.pebble --id <linkId>\n\nDEPRECATE (the \"delete\"):\n\n    pebbles-cli set-status structures/customer-dto.pebble deprecated\n\n## Method lives elsewhere\n\nThis doc DEFINES the components. HOW to fill them from a codebase\n(extraction) or prove them against it (verification) lives in the\n**extraction-by-kind** and **verification-model** docs, which reference the\ncategories above.",
    "kind": "text"
  },
  "createdAt": "2026-07-27T15:39:02.144Z",
  "description": "The component CATALOG of a Structure pebble (an in-code data shape — DTO, type, interface, payload, config, wire/return body — NOT a persisted DB table): every part and WHAT belongs under it — pebble level (name, status, description, checklist / structure / findings references), each field/property's categories (name, type + itemType, required, accepted, sample, status, description, children), the ONE reference kind (structure→structure via ref/typeRef), and every structure-related pebbles-cli command. Sibling of model-reference; structures differ (no PK, no reference key / FK, no default, no relationships). A DEFINITION reference skills point at to learn what goes under each category.",
  "id": "cd210353-7169-4f76-aceb-cfdb95fb2e27",
